From: fexdroid
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/common: add patch-id wildcard fallback for Adreno 840 (KGSL), after A840v2

The v37 variant's copy of mesa-patches/0001-freedreno-a840-kgsl-patchid-wildcard.patch
(same entry, same comment, MIT, local fexdroid patch, not upstream). The original does
not apply after the V37 recipe: v37/a840v2.py inserts the "Adreno (TM) 840v2" entries
right below the 0xffff44050A31 line, where the original's context is.

It is not redundant with a840v2.py: that adds exactly one more revision (chip_id
0x44050A21); this entry is the 0xff patch-id wildcard (dev_id_compare, case b) that binds
every other 0x44050Axx revision to the A840 properties. It is listed last in the add_gpus
group, so exact entries still win and it only names what nothing else matched.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1627,6 +1627,12 @@
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050A31, name="Adreno (TM) 840"),
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050A21, name="Adreno (TM) 840v2"),
         GPUId(chip_id=0x44050A21, name="Adreno (TM) 840v2"), # KGSL
+        # KGSL (Android) reports the 32-bit chip id; the proprietary driver on a
+        # Galaxy S26 Ultra reports 0x44050A31, which the entry above already
+        # matches once the fuse-id wildcard is applied.  Keep a patch-id
+        # wildcard fallback for other A840 revisions/SKUs so they are not
+        # rejected as "unsupported" outright (the name makes this visible).
+        GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050Aff, name="Adreno (TM) 840 (unknown patchid)"),
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A8XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2,
